"""The onboarding desk (Stage 10, spec §5.9.4): the ``onboard_step`` activity's real handler.

The ``Onboarding`` workflow runs O1–O7 as seven ``onboard_step(host, step)`` activities. Each
activity may run in a different worker process, so a host's onboarding is a **case folder**
(``<root>/<host>/``, outside every repository): ``case.json`` (registered once: the intake form,
the checkout, the maintainers' trace export, the package and its side-effecting tools) and one
``<step>.json`` per finished step, which later steps read.

| Step | What it does (offline, nothing leaves the machine) |
|---|---|
| O1 Intake | parses the Clinic form strictly; every consent box; foreign → PR-only |
| O2 Sandbox | copies the checkout into the case's sandbox (never the maintainers' repository), lists its dependency manifests and digests the tree; dependencies are installed only by an ``installer`` port (the gVisor sandbox runner in live mode) |
| O3 Instrument | the static health card; when neatlogs is not initialised, a deterministic instrumentation patch (init before any model import) is applied to the **sandbox copy only** and kept as ``instrument.patch`` |
| O4 Entire | ``entire graph snapshot`` of the sandbox: files, symbols, relations (skipped, and saying so, without entire-graph) |
| O5 Eval synthesis | seed evals from the exported traces' true failures (transient retries are not seeds), the checkout's existing tests, README examples and doctest docstrings; a deterministic 70/30 train/holdout split and the holdout manifest's sha256 |
| O6 Baseline | pass rate with its Wilson interval, cost and p95 duration of the exported traces (replay mode: they are read like live traces) |
| O7 Immune scan | every ACTIVE antibody motif against the sandbox's graph; the receipt's shipping terms (PR-only on a foreign repository, never a merge) |
"""

from __future__ import annotations

